From 3b0f43968a4370f880e5ebace6cda8947412ecce Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "William Mark Katzenmeyer, P.E., C.F.M." <heccommander@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 06:15:30 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 10/14] hdf5-reader: share one link walk across a soft/external
 link resolution

[L11] Status vs upstream v0.9.3: NOT UPSTREAM (v0.9.3 overflows the stack).
Kind: safety fix. Proposed upstream grouping: PR-B hardening.
Applies on roteiro-gis/netcdf-rust v0.9.3 (3d708fd) after the earlier patches of this series.

Soft-link resolution restarted the depth count for every intermediate
component of the target path, so a soft link '/s -> /s/x' recursed until
the stack overflowed (a 195-byte file). Carry one LinkWalk through
intermediate components and external links: one depth limit (16), an
active-link cycle guard, and an expansion budget (1024) per top-level
resolution so non-cyclic fan-out cannot grow exponentially.
